\ A wrong twin: by-focus need not close its goal, so the goal it leaves
\ comes back first and the proof's end is Lean's unsolved goals (89) at
\ by, with both goals (plan row TB2, blocks slice 1; blocks-1-wrong.lean).
\ Lean: theorem w_focus_open (a b : Nat) (h : a = b) (k : b = a) : a = b ∧ b = a := by
\         constructor
\         focus
\           have x : a = b := h
theorem w_focus_open
  Nat explicit: a  Nat explicit: b
  a b = explicit: h  b a = explicit: k
  a b = b a = ∧
:= by
  by-constructor
  by-focus a b = ' h by-have: x by-end
end w_focus_open
